          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A notion of
            %em dimension
            is a notion of “size” of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
          %h3#of_spaces Of spaces
          %p
            There are many notions of
            %em dimension
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+space"} cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            has dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong dimension
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
                of any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+of+a+vector+space"} linear basis
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is the
                = succeed "-indexed" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+theorem"} basis theorem
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                over
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
                that are not
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
                (for which the theorem above does not hold, neither existence nor uniqueness) the term used is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
                of a the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
                on a vector space coincides with its categorical trace in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %li
              %p
                Generalizing from this example, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
                of an object in a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+category"} spherical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+category"} fusion category
                is called its
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+dimension"} quantum dimension
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                has
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension of a manifold
                equal to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                if it is locally isomorphic to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
                is of
                %strong complex dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                if it is locally isomorphic to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^n
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 n
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                has (Lebesgue)
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+dimension"} covering dimension
                less than
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                if every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                such that every element of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                belongs to fewer than
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n + 1
                elements of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                has dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                if it has dimension less than
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n + 1
                but not less than
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+thinking"} negative thinking
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq -1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+space"} empty space
                has dimension
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
                (of course) has dimension
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
                has
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+CW-complex"} dimension of a CW-complex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                for which there are nontrivial
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cells"} cells
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
                has a
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+dimension"} Hausdorff dimension
                which may be any non-negative real number.
            %li
              %p
                A space in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+geometry"} spectral geometry
                via
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-dimension"} KO-dimension
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+dimension"} cohomology dimension
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+dimension"} Heyting dimension
          %h3#of_objects_in_an_abelian_category_length Of objects in an abelian category: Length
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length+of+an+object"} length of an object
          %h3#of_objects_in_a_symmetric_monoidal_category_euler_characteristic Of objects in a symmetric monoidal category: Euler characteristic
          %p
            The dimension of a (finite dimensional)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            (which is a linear map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \to k
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  tr(V) := tr(Id_V) : k \to V \otimes V^* \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} V^* \otimes V \to k
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore it makes sense for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to call
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr(Id_V) : 1 \to 1
            the
            %em
              categorical trace of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            This definition subsumes standard notions of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            and hence may also be thought of as generalizing that notion.
          %h3#of_objects_in_an_topos
            Of objects in an
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The following notions of dimension capture aspects of the concept for objects in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            or more generally an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomological+dimension"} cohomological dimension
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+dimension"} covering dimension
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+dimension"} Heyting dimension
          %h3#frobeniusperron_dimension Frobenius-Perron dimension
