          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+dimension+theorem"} global dimension theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+invariance+of+dimension"} topological invariance of dimension
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                notion of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+dimension"} cohomology dimension
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+cohomological+dimension"}> virtual
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+dimension"} covering dimension
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+dimension"} Heyting dimension
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension of a manifold
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+cell+complex"} dimension of a cell complex
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+separable+metric+space"} dimension of a separable metric space
              %li
                %p
                  small
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+dimension"} inductive dimension
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular space
              %li
                %p
                  large
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+dimension"} inductive dimension
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+space"} normal space
          %h2#references References
          %p
            For the dimension in symmetric monoidal categories see the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
          %p
            A general abstract
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theoretic
            discussion of notions of homotopy/cohomology/covering
            %em dimension
            is in section 7.2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
